  "details": "I'm not sure how technologically feasible this idea is, but I really dislike it when an avatar has an effect on the view I see in VR. I don't want anyone to shake or jiggle or give a drunk wobble to my camera. \n\nThe content tagging of such shaders may be sufficient, especially if users can report such avatars in a way that causes them to be flagged. But I had a thought to ask if the shader scanning that happens can be used to detect the effects early.",
